// Homepage poster set — the six Top Speed posters Ramone approved
// from his mockup (built for the topspeedappliance.net homepage,
// 2026-11-16; placed on the flagship Service OS homepage the same
// night at his direction: "On top speed service os homepage").
//
// Each export is the WebP bytes of one poster from
// ~/workspace/net-tiles-work/finals/<file>.webp, embedded as base64
// text because the GitHub connector is TEXT-ONLY for file writes —
// real .webp binaries cannot be pushed as files. This is the same
// pattern as platformImages.js / serviceImages.js / mascotImages.js.
//
// Served by GET /api/v1/app/poster-images/:name in routes/app.js
// (filename -> export map there); web pages reference the posters
// same-origin via /api/v1/app/poster-images/<file> (vercel.json
// rewrite on the web project).
//
// FORMAT WARNING: every export is Buffer.from( 'chunk' + 'chunk' +
// 'lastchunk', 'base64', ) — string CONCATENATION (' +' line endings,
// 100-char chunks, last chunk ends with ','). NEVER comma-separate
// the chunks: Node would read chunk #2 as an encoding and the whole
// API crashes at import (ERR_UNKNOWN_ENCODING). Always verify by
// IMPORTING this module in node and MD5-checking every export
// against its source .webp file — `node --check` does NOT catch
// the broken form.

